ey started off with the classic  hellotext from the original mac  they even used screenshots from that  colorful hello text  as the wallpapers for the imacs  themselves  and in their new imac ads they actually  brought back  a redesigned version of the rainbow  apple logo  so apple is obviously going retro and in  terms of the imac itself  apple is obviously doing a sequel to  their iconic imac g3s  from way back in the day with white  bezels and  a bunch of colors and all of this is  being done to make the apple silicon  transition  a really really big deal because it is  and the best way to make it a big deal  is to totally change  everything about the imac and make it as  obvious as possible  that these new macs are nothing like the  old max  and if you think about it it might seem  really weird that apple is giving  the same exact m1 chip to a bunch of  different products  including the ipad pro but what they're  actually doing  is pure genius apple wants that  m1 chip to essentially go viral  because the m1 chip is the symbol of the  apple silicon transition  so if the m1 chip goes viral then the  apple silicon transition goes viral  and the new drastically changed designs  will push  the importance of the transition and  this is finally where the macbook air  redesign  with white bezels comes in a big point  that i want to make is that when apple  changes things up in terms of the design  other products usually follow for  example the 2018 ipad pro got a  redesigned with flat sides  and then the pro display xdr followed  and then the ipad  air followed and then the iphone  followed  and now the imac is following that same  design language  so if the 24 inch imac ends up being the  only mac  or modern apple device with white bezels  that would be extremely weird and random  for apple to do  it's much more likely the apple will  bring these white bezels and various  color options  down to the macbook air which is  essentially the portable  version of the 24 inch imac since both  machines are targeted toward  the younger and more average consumer  market and if you think that that would  be weird for apple to do  check this out because it'll blow your  mind here's an image of the original  imac g3 colors  and this is actually the ibook g3  which was apple's laptop based on that  imac  with the same colors and all and guess  what  they've got white bezels and color  matched accessories  just like apple has on the new 24-inch  imac as well  and take a look at this ad for a newer  white macbook  the totally white macbook for everyone  yes  it's meant for the entry-level market so  if apple is going  full on retro with this imac to  symbolize the transition  then why stop at just the imac and if  you think that i'm alone in thinking  this way  i'm actually not parker over at 95 mac  wrote an  article saying that it's time for the  macbook air to get its ibook moment  and looking at this image it totally  makes sense the concepts he created are  basically  exactly what i can imagine the  redesigned new macbook to look like  white bezels with a white keyboard as  well as a bunch of different color  options  just like we have on the imac and from  taking a look at the comments  there are people who actually like the  idea of a macbook  with white bezels and here's another  very telling hint  from apple that basically puts the nail  in the coffin for the first time ever  apple has released a totally white magic  keyboard case for the ipad pro  which nobody was expecting and this is  obviously hinting  at white macbooks coming in the future  so if apple really wants their new  redesigned macbook air with apple  silicon to look different  the absolute best way to do that is to  add new colors  and make the bezels and the keyboard  white just like on the 24 inch imac  everyone will instantly be able to tell  that you have a brand new  apple silicon macbook air and that is  apple's ultimate goal  even if some people absolutely hate the  design this will just end up making more  controversy  which will result in free marketing for  apple and if you think about it  almost every laptop on the market right  now has black  bezels so if apple gave the macbook air  white bezels  it would be totally unique and it would  push the apple silicon transition  like nothing else would which is apple's  number one goal  and once again it would be extremely  weird for apple to randomly go retro  with white bezels on just the imac and  stop  there and if any other product was going  to follow in its footsteps  it would 100 percent be the entry-level  macbook air redesign  and going even deeper if they're going  to totally redesign the macbook air and  reinvented  why not just give it the original  macbook name  to kickstart a whole new generation of  macbooks  ever since the 12-inch macbook was  discontinued we've been left with the  perfect and original macbook name  which isn't being used and i don't think  the apple will introduce  a small 12-inch laptop ever again just  based on the fact that the iphone 12  mini  is not selling well at all so people  aren't looking for small displays  anymore  so let's just say that apple calls it  the macbook gives it the white bezels  the fun colors the new m2 chip and  bam you've got a killer laptop for a  great price  and it looks like nothing else on the  market now with all that said  i want to finish up with some leaks and  rumors that point to the potential  release date of this macbook  back in january mark german from  bloomberg reported that apple could  launch a new thinner and lighter  redesigned high-end macbook air with mac  safe  in the second half of 2021 he said that  apple is planning on keeping the display  size the same  but shrinking the bezels to make the  overall design smaller and thinner  which goes to show that the 12 inch  macbook is probably gone for good  now ming chi kuo another reliable apple  analyst  believes that apple is more likely to  release this macbook air  sometime in 2022 with a new design  an apple silicon chip and a new mini led  display  and digitimes another publication agreed  with this  saying that the redesigned macbook pros  would be getting mini led  first in 2021 and then that mini led  would trickle down to the macbook air in  2022  and this makes total sense to me since  they would want to give that new midi  led display  to the pro level macbooks first and on  top of that  i believe that the next generation m2  chip isn't going to be ready until  next year since i think it's gonna come  with the same  four plus four core layouts as the m1  currently has  but it's gonna rely on the new rv9  architectural  improvements and a smaller three  nanometer or four nanometer chip  architecture from tsmc to give it more  performance and battery life  and as far as the pricing i think that  it's going to start at around  twelve hundred dollars since that's what  they did in the past with the redesigned  2018 macbook air and then they'll leave  the m1 macbook air with the old design  for 999 for at least  another full year as a budget option so  there you guys have it  those are my thoughts on why the new  macbook air is gonna have  white bezels and if you totally disagree  with me  go ahead and comment your thoughts down  below but if you enjoyed this video go  ahead and click the circle about to  subscribe  for more videos like this one definitely  check out one of those two videos right  there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video
 

